Z||000018||Jay||11-04-2001||06:38 PM||||Well, my rev limiter is being a real pain in the a$$!  That's next on the list of things to do!  It seems that the ECM cuts power at a lowely 5500rpms.  I guess the Cadillac designers didn't want to give these old men heart attacks.  I've got someone working on this as we speak.<BR> I ran 13.7's all day in Time trials.  Come to the event and I broke out on my first run with a 13.5!  Banditbalz went through to the next round only to lose in the  finals to Miriame and her 2.8 turbo.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Old Lar||11-04-2001||06:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B><BR> I ran 13.7's all day in Time trials.  Come to the event and I broke out on my first run with a 13.5!  Banditbalz went through to the next round only to lose in the  finals to Miriame and her 2.8 turbo.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Was it her 2.8 turbo or 3.1 turbo?  Joe has the touch for building those cars.||||reg||1
Z||000020||banditbalz||11-04-2001||06:53 PM||||JM, was a great day! More Fieros attended than was expected. Jay's N* was running good, but unsure of his best time. I ran him once and it was unbelievable how quick his car will pull away from me at half track. God his car looks sweet from the ass end!<P>The best I could muster was a 15.20 at 89 mp/h. Hit this number 3 times. And a new best '60 time of 1.937. I was running very consistant all day. Even took an Integra Type R. <BR>I ran once against Tim (2.8 auto w/NOS). My 15.3@88 to his 15.4@88<P>In eliminations, I ran Jay and we both broke out of our dial in times (it was really cold. cold air = horsepower).  But, I got the win on account Jay red lighted. I guess they don't recognize a double breakout?<P>In final eliminations (not sure of the prize, but may have been as much as $400), I was up against Mireamme (turbo 3.1, 4 speed). She was running 13.8 most of the day. In all the excitement, I launched a little early and red lighted. From first gear, I  shut her down and coasted to a 27 sec. quarter. <P>It turned out to be a good day. We had support from XthumperX (4 speed 2M4) and The owners of Racetech (including a mechanic) were there. <P>I am getting tired of hitting low 15's all day. Need NOS...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000021||banditbalz||11-04-2001||07:07 PM||||Forgot to mention, Lothar hit a new best of 15.1 @ 91 mp/h in his black 88GT 2.8 turbo. I think Joe got all the carbon out when he did a run just before...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000022||Slammed Fiero||11-04-2001||08:14 PM||||I hope all the magazine readin Nay sayers read this..<P>15.20 STCOK FIERO!<P>GIDDY UP!<P>Good job Guys. hopefully I will be able to come and play next year. 15.4 with nos?? is that a 5hp shot?<P>sorry had to  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000023||Shaun41178||11-04-2001||08:33 PM||||yea no kidding a 15.4 with using nitrous on a v6?  I never ran a 15 second qr mile time in my fiero when using NOS.  Well I will correct that I did once but I turned the nitrous off at the 60' mark and I ended up running a 15.8.<P><BR>Something is wrong with that car.  I know I have said it before as I have seen it mentioned here before but what is the matter with that car?  Why is it so slow?<P>Also why is that turbo 88Gt only able to muster a 15.1?  how much boost is he guy running?  How can a stock Fiero run a 15.2 and a turbo one only turn a 15.1?  ARe the drivers that bad?  Is Banditbalz that good?<P>Come on explain something to me.  I mean I ran a 14.2 with my auto 2.8 with nitrous.  internally stock.  Help me understand this please.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000024||Slammed Fiero||11-04-2001||10:52 PM||||According to the guy wh owns it , it's a 3.2! he has a 3800 Tq converter which is not a good idea (IMHO) Really nice clean car , but for some reason slow as all Hell. I don't have th epicin front of me , but he has a sign that goes in front of his car , says crane came , 1.6 rockers ,ported heads..blah blah blah..the usual performance build up goodies. Personally i think It should be a mid 13 sec car with nos .<P>just my 2 cents<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Jay||11-04-2001||11:01 PM|||| 15.4 with NOS?... I've got one word for you...Bad driver...okay it was two words.  But I'll be willing to put money on it that another driver in the same car would turn at least low 14's<P>A Honda civic hatchback did a mid 9 second run today at over 153mph.  That was cool.||||reg||1
Z||000026||AkursedX||11-05-2001||12:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Shaun41178:<BR><B><P>Also why is that turbo 88Gt only able to muster a 15.1?  how much boost is he guy running?  How can a stock Fiero run a 15.2 and a turbo one only turn a 15.1?  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>George's GT is a Stock 86 4-speed, and Lothar's Turbo is an 88 Auto.  I think it is running 8lbs of boost.  <P>The gearing is a HUGE difference, and 88's are also heavier than the previous years, and George is also that good of a driver.<P><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Brandon86SE||11-05-2001||01:00 AM||||My best run in my stock 2.8 is 15.333 with a 2.551 60'.  It is my understanding that the 85/86 V6 4 speeds are actually the fastest Fiero's, because of the gearing.  I only shift twice in the 1/4, finish in 3rd.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000028||artherd||11-05-2001||01:16 AM||||Jay, that rev limiter shouldn't be kicking in untill *6750* rpm!!!<P>Heck, the N*'s *power peak* occurs at 6,000....  (and it's 'red line' is 6500.  Rev limiter kicks in 250rpm later to prevent fragging)<P>Maybe you're still in one of the many 'something ain't right, I gonna go slower' ECM modes?<P>Wow, can't wait to see what that car will do once you can wind it out. (supposedly the limiting factor in revs is actually our cylinder heads.  Lifters and springs specifically.  Bottom end is supposed to be good to 8grand(!!!), says Chrfab.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>Well, my rev limiter is being a real pain in the a$$!  That's next on the list of things to do!  It seems that the ECM cuts power at a lowely 5500rpms.  I guess the Cadillac designers didn't want to give these old men heart attacks.  I've got someone working on this as we speak.<BR> I ran 13.7's all day in Time trials.  Come to the event and I broke out on my first run with a 13.5!  Banditbalz went through to the next round only to lose in the  finals to Miriame and her 2.8 turbo.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000029||Jay||11-05-2001||09:54 AM||||artherd, I've got the dash from the STS in my car.  It shows yellow at 5000rpm and redline at 5500.  I get up to 5000 in a real hurry, and that's what I can't understand.  I'm running out of rev's about 20 feet before the finish line!  I know it is the right dash.  You need it to scan the ECM, and it does scan.  The ECM is slave to the chip in the dash, without it you will not get any info out of the ECM.  This is strange.||||reg||1
