Z||000034||NOS3800||11-06-2001||12:08 AM||||Great times guys, we have three 3800's going to Maryland International raceway this weekend. I  will post and we can compare times. The times for the NOS 2.8 and Turbo 88 seem slow. You can't messup too much with an auto, you just need to keep the car straight. I think some tuning is in order! <BR>Jay, look into your car. I know that if the N* is overheating it cuts back on spark, may be your problem, or your car is in a PCM program that has put the car into limp home mode. Just because the Engine Service light is not on doesn't mean the code isn't there.<BR>I had a similar problem with mine, but it was shifting at 4500rpm. It had a code for the Trans( high heat mode). Do not know why it was there, possibly from the accident the donor car was in. Once it was erased, the shift point raised to 5800. Over the summer the car started doing it again, especially on hot days. There was no code, but I stumbled upon the fact that my heater core hoses where hooked up wrong, not allowing proper coolant flow. MOtor didn't like this. Once I got it fixed, ran the fastest times without NOS since the conversion. Look into your coolant flow, your car may be getting heat spikes and cutting back on the spark to save the motor.<BR>Just some tips.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000035||NOS3800||11-06-2001||12:09 AM||||Great times guys, we have three 3800's going to Maryland International raceway this weekend. I  will post and we can compare times. The times for the NOS 2.8 and Turbo 88 seem slow. You can't messup too much with an auto, you just need to keep the car straight. I think some tuning is in order! <BR>Jay, look into your car. I know that if the N* is overheating it cuts back on spark, may be your problem, or your car is in a PCM program that has put the car into limp home mode. Just because the Engine Service light is not on doesn't mean the code isn't there.<BR>I had a similar problem with mine, but it was shifting at 4500rpm. It had a code for the Trans( high heat mode). Do not know why it was there, possibly from the accident the donor car was in. Once it was erased, the shift point raised to 5800. Over the summer the car started doing it again, especially on hot days. There was no code, but I stumbled upon the fact that my heater core hoses where hooked up wrong, not allowing proper coolant flow. MOtor didn't like this. Once I got it fixed, ran the fastest times without NOS since the conversion. Look into your coolant flow, your car may be getting heat spikes and cutting back on the spark to save the motor.<BR>Just some tips.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
